# What the vendored build makes of the sources, none of it belonging in git.
# tools/vendor.sh writes the archive at release time and it travels inside the
# source tarball, which is why it is deliberately absent from .Rbuildignore and
# present here; a routine `git add -A` after running that script would otherwise
# commit several megabytes that change with every dependency bump. The other two
# are what the install recipe makes of the archive.
rust/vendor.tar.xz
rust/vendor/
rust/.cargo-vendor/
